<title>SPAIN: BASKETBALL-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>GERONA, Spain 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Final standings after the</p>
<p>first group phase of the European basketball championship ending</p>
<p>on Friday:</p>
<p>			   P     W    L   F    A</p>
<p> 1. Greece	     3     3    0  226  200</p>
<p> 2. Russia	     3     2    1  224  185</p>
<p> 3. Turkey	     3     1    2  178  223</p>
<p> 4. Bosnia	     3     0    3  193  213</p>
<p>Bosnia are eliminated with the other three teams progressing</p>
<p>to the second phase.</p>
<p>Group D:</p>
<p>			   P     W    L   F    A</p>
<p> 1. Spain		3     3    0  227  184</p>
<p> 2. Croatia	    3     1    2  234  228</p>
<p> 3. Germany	    3     1    2  195  202</p>
<p> 4. Ukraine	    3     1    2  209  251</p>
<p>Spain, Croatia and Germany go through to second phase,</p>
<p>Ukraine are eliminated.</p>
<p>Group C final standings:</p>
<p>		     Pl     W    L   pf   pa</p>
<p> Italy		3     3    0  239  209</p>
<p> Yugoslavia	 3     2    1  281  239</p>
<p> Poland	     3     1    2  227  263</p>
<p> Latvia	     3     0    3  243  279</p>
<p>Latvia are eliminated.  The other three teams go through to the next round.</p>
<p>Group B final standings:</p>
<p>		     Pl     W    L   pf   pa</p>
<p> Lithuania	  3     3    0  245  215</p>
<p> Israel	     3     2    1  217  225</p>
<p> France	     3     1    2  250  257</p>
<p> Slovenia	   3     0    3  210  225</p>
<p>Slovenia are eliminated. The other three teams go through to the next round.</p>
